---
// The about page's text in English. Its layout and styles are in
// src/pages/[lang]/about.astro; every language needs its own file here.
import { getRelativeLocaleUrl } from "astro:i18n";
import { boardPath } from "../../../data/nav";
import { contactEmail, owner, ownerUrl } from "../../../data/site";

interface Props {
  lang: string;
}

const { lang } = Astro.props;
---

<p class="lead">A tactics board for handball coaches, made by a handball coach.</p>

<h2>What it does</h2>
<ul>
  <li>
    Draw an attack, a defense or a drill on <a href={getRelativeLocaleUrl(lang, boardPath)}>the board</a>,
    on a half or a full court.
  </li>
  <li>Drag your players into place and draw runs, passes and dribbles.</li>
  <li>
    Share your drawing with your team, as a link or QR code. Your players see it on their own phone,
    without an app or account.
  </li>
  <li>
    Browse the <a href={getRelativeLocaleUrl(lang, "tactics/")}>tactics</a> and <a
      href={getRelativeLocaleUrl(lang, "drills/")}>drills</a>. Open one in the board and adapt it for
    your team.
  </li>
</ul>

<h2>What the board can do</h2>
<ul>
  <li><strong>Drawing arrows.</strong> The board opens with Arrow on: drag from a player for a run, and from the ball for a pass.</li>
  <li><strong>Kinds of arrow.</strong> Tap an arrow and pick run, pass, bounce, dribble, shot or screen.</li>
  <li><strong>Shooting.</strong> A pass that ends between the posts is a shot.</li>
  <li><strong>Starting lineups.</strong> On a new board, set out a lineup in one tap: against 6-0, 5-1 or 3-2-1, or two or three lines for a drill.</li>
  <li><strong>Steps.</strong> Tap New step for the next step and type one sentence per step: who does what.</li>
  <li><strong>Play.</strong> Tap the button next to New step: the players move along their arrows, step by step.</li>
  <li><strong>My boards.</strong> More holds your boards, saved in this browser, in folders in the order of your practice.</li>
  <li><strong>Sharing.</strong> Everything is in the link or in the QR code in More, so your players see every step with its sentence, without an account or app.</li>
</ul>

<h2>Free, without an account</h2>
<p>
  The board is free. You and your players don't need an account. There are no cookies and no ads.
  The <a href={getRelativeLocaleUrl(lang, "privacy/")}>privacy page</a> explains what happens to
  your drawings.
</p>

<section id="contact">
  <h2>Contact</h2>
  <p>
    Handball Coachboard is made by <a href={ownerUrl}>{owner}</a>. A question or an idea?
    Email <a href={`mailto:${contactEmail}`}>{contactEmail}</a>.
  </p>
</section>
